.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SS "template<uint32_t dim>
.br
class csmp::CVFEM_PressureGradientVisitor< dim >"Calculating the pressure gradient within the CVFEM scheme (Weis et al\&., Geofluids, 2014)\&.

.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
Philipp Weis, ETH Zuerich 
.RE
.PP
.SH "Contact"
.PP
philipp.weis@erdw.ethz.ch

.PP
@changes changes Latest Changes
.SH "Motivation"
.PP
For the fully-upwinded scheme including fluid viscosity and relative permeability, the CVFEM scheme needs the varibale KgradP instead of velcotities to perform the finite volume calculations\&.
.SH "Usage"
.PP
Used within the CVFEM scheme (Weis et al\&., Geofluids, 2014)\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
The visitor calculates the pressure gradient at the elements barycenter from the nodal variable "fluid pressure"\&.
This vector variable is multiplied with the element permeability k\&.
k * grad( P )
.fi
.PP
.SH "Dependencies"
.PP
.SH "Known issues"
.PP
The variable gradp_scaling is not well documented and only needed in combination with the permeability vistor\&. The bool gradient_scaling can't be changed from outside\&.
.SH "Testing"
.PP
testing was done in the period before publication in 2014\&. 
